      "id": "GENUS_LANIUS",
      "name": "Lanius",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "The typical shrikes — passerine birds of open country with a hooked bill and a raptor-like hunting style. Shrikes earned the name 'butcher birds' from their habit of impaling prey on thorns and barbed wire as a larder. Despite being songbirds, they hunt insects, small mammals, lizards, and even other birds, striking from exposed perches with surgical precision. The genus is widely distributed across Eurasia, Africa, and North America.",
